{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 640,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you stayed at your job for the last \n5 years because you like the culture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you value loyalty, I have some \nuncomfortable news. You didn't just stay.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You essentially wrote your boss a check for \n$50,000 and told them to keep the change.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18560,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We like to think of loyalty as a two-way street, \na mutual pact between a hardworking professional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24920,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a company that appreciates them. But in \nthe cold, hard world of corporate finance,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30800,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "loyalty is often treated as a line item on \na spreadsheet titled avoidable expenses.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37240,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your company has a specific \nbudget for people like you,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40400,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is designed to be as small as possible. \nMeanwhile, they have a completely different budget  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the person they're going to hire to sit \nin the desk next to yours. And that budget,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52200,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's significantly larger. Today, we're going \nto dismantle the myth of the steady 3% raise  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59560,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and look at why your HR department is quietly \nhoping you never check your market value.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65720,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've run the numbers and the gap between \na loyal stayer and a strategic job hopper  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't just a few extra dollars for a vacation. \nIt is the difference between retiring in comfort  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76480,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or working an extra decade just to keep up \nwith the cost of groceries. Before we dive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the math that proves your boss is counting \non your inertia, I want to make a deal with you.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most personal finance advice tells you how to \nsave $10 on your coffee or how to clip coupons.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95120,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think your time is worth more than that. This \nanalysis is about the earning side of the ledger,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the single most powerful \nlever you have for building wealth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105200,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you find this breakdown helpful, consider \nhitting the subscribe button. It is probably  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110200,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the best return on investment for 20 minutes \nof your time that you will find all week.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115600,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I spent a dozen hours digging through Federal \nReserve data and labor statistics so you don't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119880,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to. We are going to look at how a simple \ndecision made every 3 years can compound into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125440,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a million dollar difference in your net worth. And \nif you really want to get into the weeds with me,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130600,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check out the join button below to become one \nof the optimizers. you get a special badge  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135920,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I prioritize your questions when we're \ndebating these strategies in the comments.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140960,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's start by looking at why your manager's hands \nare often tied, even if they actually like you.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148120,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the world of corporate finance, money \nisn't just one big pile. It is divided into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very specific silos. You have the retention \nbudget and the talent acquisition budget.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161160,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think of the retention budget \nas the maintenance fund.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the money set aside to give existing \nemployees their annual cost of living adjustments.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Usually, this pool is capped at three or \nmaybe 4% of the total department payroll.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your manager has 10 employees and they want to \ngive one of them a real life-changing 10% raise,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184280,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they have to effectively steal that money from \nthe other nine people. It's a zero- sum game  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190280,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "played in a very small sandbox. This creates \nsomething called wage compression. Over time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more experience you gain at a single company, \nthe less each year of that experience is actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203280,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worth in dollar terms. You are becoming more \nvaluable to the company every day, but your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "salary is anchored to the number you negotiated \nyears ago when you knew less and had fewer skills.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215880,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a fundamental mismatch between your \nvalue and your paycheck that only grows wider  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the longer you stay in that swivel chair. \nNow compare that tiny retention sandbox  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226720,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the talent acquisition budget. This is \nthe emergency fund. When a role sits empty,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233000,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company loses money. Operations slow down, \nprojects stall, and everyone else gets stressed.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240320,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To fix this, HR looks at the open market. They \ndon't care what you were making 3 years ago.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246480,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They care what it takes to get a \nqualified person in that seat today.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the market rate for your job has jumped \n20% because of a talent shortage or inflation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256120,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company will pay it. They have to. This leads \nto the incredibly frustrating scenario where a new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263080,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hire walks in the door with half your experience \nbut a salary that's 15% higher than yours.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Harvard Business Review actually looked \ninto this and found that external hires  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273520,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are consistently paid more than internal \npromotions for the same level of responsibility.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279280,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your company is essentially paying a new person \npremium while charging you a loyalty tax.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284960,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They know that if they can keep \nyou from looking at the job boards,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can continue to buy your labor at a \nsteep discount. Your inertia is literally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidizing their profit margins, and they aren't \ngoing to volunteer to stop that arrangement.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299160,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might wonder why companies take the risk \nof losing good people by underpaying them.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305200,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer lies in behavioral economics \nand something called switching costs.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311080,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your boss knows that changing jobs is a \nmassive pain. You have to update your resume,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316880,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "handle awkward networking calls, sit through \nfour rounds of interviews, and then face the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322440,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "terrifying new kid feeling of a first day at a \nnew office. You have social capital where you are.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330480,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know where the good coffee is and which \nmanagers to avoid. That comfort has a price tag.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists have found that most people \nwill accept being underpaid by 10 to 15%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343480,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just to avoid the stress of a move. Employers \ncount on this psychological friction.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They offer a 3% raise because it feels like \nsomething and it's usually just enough to keep you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356560,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from walking into your boss office to quit. It's \nthe corporate version of the boiling frog fable.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363680,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The water gets slightly more expensive every \nyear, but never quite hot enough to make you jump.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370200,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you want to build real wealth, you have to \nstop thinking of your job as a family relationship  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376160,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and start thinking of it as a business \ntransaction. You are a corporation of one and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382360,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are currently selling your product to a buyer \nwho is refusing to pay the current market price.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To beat the loyalty penalty, you have to \nadopt the mindset of a free agent. Imagine  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a professional athlete. Do they stay with the team \nfor 20 years out of the goodness of their heart?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401000,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, they stay if the team pays the market rate and \nthey test the market when their contract is up.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409120,
    "dDurationMs": 8120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are the CEO of your own career. Your human \ncapital is the most valuable asset you own. If you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417240,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were running a literal business and one of your \nclients insisted on paying 2019 prices in 2024,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423720,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would drop that client in a heartbeat. Yet, \nwhen it comes to our salaries, we get emotional.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430320,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We feel like we owe the company something \nbecause they gave us a chance. Here's the truth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435640,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They didn't give you a gift. They bought your time \nbecause they expected to make a profit from it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The moment you stop being profitable, they will \nlet you go without a second thought. By staying  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446520,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a submarket raise, you are effectively giving \nthem a charitable donation that you didn't intend  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451720,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make. In the next section, I'm going to show \nyou the actual math of what this looks like over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457640,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "15 years. I've built a case study comparing two \npeople, and the result is frankly staggering.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you think a few percent here and there doesn't \nmatter, wait until you see the cumulative gap.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470760,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's put some hard numbers on this. I want to \nintroduce you to two hypothetical professionals,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476920,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sarah and David. They both start their \ncareers at age 25, earning $70,000 a year.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484760,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sarah is our loyal stayer. She \nloves her team. She does great work,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and every year she gets a standard 3% merit \nincrease. She's happy because she's moving up.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David, on the other hand, is our strategic \nhopper. He isn't job hopping every 6 months,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which would be a red flag. Instead, he \nstays for 3 years, learns everything he can,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510640,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then moves to a new company for a 20% raise. \nTo keep the math conservative, we'll assume David  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets zero raises while he's at a company. \nHe only gets that big jump when he switches.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524400,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After 15 years, Sarah has been a \ndedicated employee at one firm.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529880,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David has worked at five different companies. On \nthe surface, they've both had successful careers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when you look at the paychecks in year 15, the \nreality of the loyalty penalty becomes undeniable.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544840,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sarah's 3% raises have compounded \nher salary to about $15,000.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551560,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That sounds pretty good, right? A $35,000 increase \nover 15 years is nothing to sneeze at. But David,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560720,
    "dDurationMs": 8600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because he captured those 20% jumps every 3 years, \nhis base salary in year 15 is over $145,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He is making $40,000 more than Sarah \nevery single year just for doing the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575680,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same level of work at a different building. \nThe annual difference is one thing, but the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581480,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cumulative total is where the loyalty penalty \nreally starts to hurt. Over those 15 years,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588280,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I calculated the total gross income for both of \nthem. Sarah earned a respectable $1.29 million,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596560,
    "dDurationMs": 9040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but David, by chasing the market rate, earned \n$1.56 million. That is a $270,000 difference.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sarah paid a quart of a million \nin loyalty tax to her employer.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about what you could \ndo with an extra $270,000.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616680,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a house paid in cash in many parts of the \ncountry. It's a college education for two kids.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624120,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a decade of early retirement. And remember, \nDavid didn't have to work harder than Sarah.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630640,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He didn't have to be a genius. He just had to be \nwilling to endure the friction of an interview  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635560,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "process every 3 years. He treated his career like \na business while Sarah treated hers like a home.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, here is where most people stop the analysis, \nbut it's actually where it gets interesting.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're a regular viewer of this channel, \nyou know I don't care about gross income.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654400,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I care about net worth. And when we look \nat how David can invest that extra money,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659720,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the numbers move from significant \nto absolutely life-changing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664200,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're going to talk about the compound interest \ngap. Next, let's assume David and Sarah live  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670080,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the exact same lifestyle. They both spend \nmoney as if they only have Sarah's income.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676280,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means David is taking that entire hopper \npremium, the extra money he makes from his raises,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681920,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and funneling it straight into a lowcost S\u0026P \n500 index fund. After accounting for taxes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David is able to invest thousands of \ndollars more every year than Sarah can.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the end of our 15-year window, his investment \naccount hasn't just grown by the amount he put in.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700200,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has grown by the power of the market.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703560,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Sarah has zero extra savings from her \nsalary increases because they barely kept up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708320,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with her lifestyle, David has built a portfolio \nworth roughly $245,000, assuming a 7% return.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they both stop working at that point and just \nlet their money sit, David's loyalty penalty  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722880,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "savings will compound into nearly a million \ndollars by the time he hits retirement age.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728720,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sarah didn't just lose $200,000 in wages. She \nlost a million dollars in future net worth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736160,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the hidden cost of staying too long. \nYou aren't just losing today's dollars. You are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741720,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losing the future versions of those dollars that \nwould have been working for you in the background.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747120,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your boss is effectively stealing your retirement \nand they're doing it with a smile and a 3% pat on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752760,
    "dDurationMs": 8560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the back. There is another hidden multiplier here \nthat most people miss. The employer 401k match.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762560,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most companies offer a match based \non a percentage of your base salary.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767680,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your company matches 4% of your pay and your \nsalary is $40,000 higher because you job hopped,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774480,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are getting an extra $1600 in \ncompletely free money every single year.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over a 30-year career, that extra matching money \nand the decades of compound interest it earns can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786960,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "easily add another $200,000 to your nest egg. It's \na double win. You earn more so you can save more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794760,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your employer is forced to give you more in \nbenefits. On the flip side, Sarah is getting a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800080,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller match on a smaller salary. She has to lock \nup a much higher percentage of her take-home pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just to hit the same retirement goals that David \nhits effortlessly. This is why I say you can't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811480,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "budget your way out of a stagnant salary. If \nSarah wants to catch up to David's savings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816560,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "she would have to live a significantly more \nrestricted life. She'd have to skip the vacations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822120,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and drive the older car, all because she didn't \nwant to deal with the hassle of a new job.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827720,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "David gets to live a better life and retire \nwealthier simply because he understood the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832240,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "math of the loyalty penalty early on. Now, we have \nto talk about the ghost in the room, inflation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840360,
    "dDurationMs": 8040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a long time, inflation was low, around 2%. In \nthat world, a 3% raise felt like a small win. You  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848400,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were gaining 1% in purchasing power every year. It \nwasn't much, but you were at least moving forward.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855960,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as we've seen in the last \nfew years, that world is gone.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860120,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If inflation is running at 5 or 6% and your \nboss gives you a 3% raise, I have news for you.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866920,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You didn't get a raise. You got a 2 or 3% pay \ncut. Your nominal salary, the number on the paper,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873680,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "went up, but your real wage, what those \ndollars can actually buy, went down.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The grocery store doesn't care about your loyalty. \nThe gas station doesn't care that you've been at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your company for 10 years. They only care \nabout the current price of the commodity.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890880,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Internal corporate budgets are incredibly slow to \nreact to inflation. They are often set 18 months  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897000,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in advance. But the external labor market, it \nreacts in real time. If you want to protect your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904040,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "standard of living during inflationary times, you \ncannot rely on the annual merit cycle. Job hopping  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't just an aggressive wealth-b buildinging \nstrategy anymore. It is a defensive necessity.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916360,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the only way to reset your wages to reflect \nthe actual cost of living in the world today.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922040,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you don't move, you are slowly but surely \nbecoming poorer every single year you stay.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929600,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't want to make it sound like job \nhopping is all sunshine and massive checks.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934600,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are risks and the biggest one is what I \ncall the vesting trap. Companies aren't stupid.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941600,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They know about the loyalty penalty and they \nuse golden handcuffs to keep you from leaving.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947760,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This usually takes the form of vesting schedules \nfor your 401k match or restricted stock units.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955440,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have $50,000 in company stock \nthat doesn't vest for another year,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving for a 20% raise might actually \ncost you money in the short term.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where you have to become a bit of \na spreadsheet warrior. Before you accept  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970760,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a new offer, you need to calculate your total \ncompensation break even point. You have to look at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977560,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what you're walking away from. Unvested matches, \npending bonuses, or even your acred vacation time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985200,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and see if the new salary covers that loss \nwithin the first 12 months. A pro tip here,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992480,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many companies are willing to offer a sign on \nbonus specifically to buy out the equity you're  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997720,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving behind, but you have to ask for it. If you \ndon't know your numbers, you can't negotiate them.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why I tell people to keep a \nrunning tally of their unvested assets.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010640,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You never want to be in a position where you're \ntoo afraid to leave because you don't understand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015120,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the math of your own exit. Loyalty should be a \nchoice, not a cage made of unvested stock options.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023640,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is also the LIFO risk, last in first out. \nWhen the economy sour and the layoffs start,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030640,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the person who has been there for 20 years \nand knows where all the bodies are buried  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035080,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is often safer than the new hire who \njust commanded a massive premium.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040440,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a job hopper, you represent a \nhigher cost on the balance sheet.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044800,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To mitigate this, you have to be two things. \nExcellent at your job and financially prepared.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You should use part of that hopper premium to \nbuild a larger than average emergency fund.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056840,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If Sarah keeps three months of expenses in \nthe bank, David should keep six or nine.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are trading the perceived security of tenure \nfor the actual security of a large cash pile.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And frankly, in the modern economy, institutional \nloyalty is a bit of an illusion. Anyway, we've  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074600,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seen loyal employees of 30 years get laid off \nvia a mass email on a Tuesday morning. The only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080800,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real security you have is your skill set and your \nbank account. By job hopping, you are diversifying  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your experience and building a network across \nmultiple companies, which actually makes you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092000,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more employable in a downturn than someone who \nonly knows how one specific company operates.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the end of the day, the company loyalty \npenalty is only a penalty if you choose to pay it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105000,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've seen how staying for a 3% raise can cost \nyou hundreds of thousands of dollars in lifetime  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110160,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earnings and millions in future net worth. We've \nseen how inflation turns loyalty into a pay cut.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116840,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your boss hopes you stay because your inertia \nmakes their job easier and their department more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121040,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profitable. But your primary fiduciary duty is to \nyourself and your family. If you haven't looked at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a job board in 3 years, do it this weekend. Not \nbecause you have to leave, but because you need  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to know what you're worth. You might find that \nyou're perfectly compensated. Or you might find  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137520,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you're effectively paying a $30,000 a year \nsubscription fee to keep your current commute.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143160,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knowledge is power. Once you know the math, \nyou can't unknow it. You can decide to stay,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149320,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it will be a conscious choice, not a default \nsetting. If you've ever negotiated a big jump or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155040,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you've been burned by staying too long, I want \nto hear about it. Let's do some peer review in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159720,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comments. Your story might be the nudge someone \nelse needs to finally stop paying the loyalty tax."
    } ]
  } ]
}
